module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_shared_cargo_target_lets_one_session_measure_anothers_compiler

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_shared_cargo_target_lets_one_session_measure_anothers_compiler: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_shared_cargo_target_lets_one_session_measure_anothers_compiler" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-09-22 (sunny-ibex-112): SAME INVALID STATE, NEW POPULATION -- THE SEED BINARY, not the probe root. /cargo-target is the cargo target directory every session in every worktree resolves by default, so `cargo build -p v1-compiler` writes /cargo-target/release/gunbc and /cargo-target/release/claim_executor for EVERYONE. Keyed by what is built, not by who builds it; second writer wins; the loser measures the winner. That is a_shared_probe_root_lets_one_run_compile_anothers_source verbatim, one layer up from the emitted probe crate: there the shared artifact is the generated SOURCE, here it is the COMPILER ITSELF.",

    "THE SPECIMEN, and it is the probe-root row's distinguishing fact firing one layer up. A repair to the FreeMonoid match lowering (gunbc#12026) was verified present in the binary by a string that exists only in the repaired code -- count 1. Four enrolled rows were then run. Two returned false. The failing fixture was emitted directly to see why, and the emitted function carried the PRE-REPAIR lowering: a two-way is_empty split, the third arm absent, a head binding referenced but never bound. The binary timestamp fell AFTER the verification. A neighbour had rebuilt v1-compiler from their own mirror in between, and every measurement after that point was a verdict about somebody else's compiler.",

    "WHAT IT NEARLY COST, recorded because the near-miss is the evidence. The output was a textbook reproduction of the very defect under repair, so the available readings were (a) file a finding that the new refusal does not cover refutable head sub-patterns, and repair working code against a phantom, or (b) loosen the two failing assertions until they matched the observed output, which manufactures a green by bending the control -- the worse branch, and the one this corpus exists to refuse. What actually broke the tie was that TWO MEASUREMENTS OF ONE FILE DISAGREED: the repair-only string counted 1 earlier and 0 later, same path. A single measurement is authoritative-looking in either direction.",

    "THREE LANES IN TWO HOURS, which is what moved this from a session mishap to an occurrence. sunny-ibex-112 as above. stern-wolf-590 read DivisionByZero out of a neighbour built binary while probing ?? semantics. bold-seal-329 was warned before it reached them and confirmed their green arm was already built into a session-private target, while noting they could no longer re-verify the red arm's target directory after the fact -- which is itself the reason the artifact-carried form below matters more than the directory discipline.",

    "THE CONSEQUENCE IS WORSE FOR A DIFFERENTIAL INSTRUMENT THAN FOR A SINGLE-ARM LANE, and bold-seal-329's oracle is the case. A single-arm lane gets a false NEGATIVE somebody eventually chases down. A two-arm differential -- interpreter against emitted binary, or broken emitter against repaired emitter -- depends on its arms coming from two SPECIFIC compilers. If a neighbour's build lands between the two emissions, BOTH ARMS BECOME THE SAME COMPILER, the differential reports no divergence, and every field of the record is well formed. The instrument built to catch confident well-formed answers about the wrong subject then produces one about itself.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, stated as the general form because the directory discipline is the weaker half: PREFER EVIDENCE THAT CARRIES ITS OWN PROVENANCE OVER EVIDENCE THAT DEPENDS ON A TOOL'S STATE AT A MOMENT. A timestamp, a symbol count, or a freshly verified binary is a claim about the INSTRUMENT, and it expires silently the moment a peer writes to the shared path. A retained artifact whose content only one producer could have written is a claim about the SUBJECT, and it stays checkable after the run that made it. Worked example from the same PR: its red control needed no binary check at all, because the baseline crate contains the two-way split and ZERO length-conditions while an enrolled row establishes that the repaired emitter must emit a length test for that exact arm shape -- so the artifact names its own producer. The two refusal rows in that PR were rewritten to the same form after bold-seal-329 asked for it.",

    "WHY THIS IS ITS OWN ROW AND NOT AN OCCURRENCE OF THE PROBE-ROOT ROW. The probe-root trigger -- probe-root selection yields an owned root, so the path and the exclusion cannot be separated -- works because a selection function exists IN THIS CORPUS to be made to return an owned root. /cargo-target has no such function: the path is chosen by an environment variable set at container setup, outside the corpus, and the writer is cargo itself. There is nothing here for us to make own the exclusion, so the construction that discharges the probe-root population leaves this one standing. That row is discharged by construction (its DISCHARGE, 2026-09-23); widening its trigger to cover this population would name more than a buildable capability, and a trigger like that is retired by nothing. So the population gets its own row and its own trigger.",

    "AND THE REMEDY THIS OCCURRENCE USED IS THE ONE THIS ROW ALREADY PRICES AS WEAK. Building into a worktree-local CARGO_TARGET_DIR is exactly that row's own `setting a per-run environment variable is a weaker mitigation still: it protects the launches that remember`. It protected this lane only because this lane now remembers, and it protects no caller who does not. Stated plainly so the workaround is not read as a repair. That row's REVIEW TELL also fires cleanly on the new population: grep the protected resource rather than the protection, and every session running a v1-compiler build is a caller of the shared resource that mentions no guard, because none exists on that path.",

    "RUNG: found BELOW the ladder -- a confident, specific verdict about a compiler other than the one under test. A lane that builds into a worktree-local CARGO_TARGET_DIR sits at 1 (mitigation that holds only for the launches that remember).",

    "CEILING 4, structurally impossible, with the reason: the corpus DOES own a route here even though it does not own the directory. gunbc.repo_self_build names the seed build command, and extdeps.rust.cargo_build models cargo's build invocation. A build route that derives its target directory from the run that invokes it -- rather than inheriting CARGO_TARGET_DIR from container setup -- makes building the seed and owning the output inseparable, the same construction that discharged the probe-root population. What remains outside the corpus is a direct `cargo build` typed by hand, which is the outside-the-modeled-guarantee column, not a ceiling.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (a CAPABILITY, not an artifact), classified CAN CLIMB NOW BUT UNBUILT: the seed build route (gunbc.repo_self_build, and every instrument that builds the seed before measuring with it) derives a run-owned target directory and hands the measuring step the binary it built, so no measurement can read a binary the run did not write. Setting CARGO_TARGET_DIR in one lane's launch does NOT discharge this row; it is the weaker mitigation recorded above.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
